WEBVTT

00:00:00.840 --> 00:00:03.050
<i>Last time on </i>Zombie Land Saga Revenge<i>,</i>

00:00:03.050 --> 00:00:05.390
<i>we did a show at the EFS, but it bombed,
 and we were in big trouble!</i>

00:00:05.390 --> 00:00:08.390
<i>We were working part-time jobs while waiting 
for Kotaro-san and his new long hair,</i>

00:00:08.390 --> 00:00:10.970
<i>but he never showed up 
and I'd finally had enough!</i>

00:00:10.970 --> 00:00:14.780
<i>We decided to put on a show to relaunch 
the group after the EFS disaster,</i>

00:00:14.780 --> 00:00:16.940
<i>and hairy Kotaro-san showed up 
just to get his butt kicked!</i>

00:00:16.940 --> 00:00:20.880
<i>Seeing that helped us get back in the groove 
and we managed to pull the show off!</i>

00:00:20.880 --> 00:00:22.710
<i>Our revenge really begins now!</i>

00:00:22.710 --> 00:00:25.950
<i>These seven lives that ended in Saga 
have been reborn with zombie bodies!</i>

00:00:25.950 --> 00:00:27.560
<i>Even if they say it can't be done, 
we'll sing and dance!</i>

00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:29.690
<i>Because if Franchouchou
can't do it, who will?!</i>

00:00:39.570 --> 00:00:40.670
What is it, Sakura?

00:00:41.840 --> 00:00:46.650
I just got kinda nervous once I realized 
we're going to be active idols again...

00:00:46.870 --> 00:00:48.090
That's okay.

00:00:48.090 --> 00:00:51.790
Getting used to things is important, 
but you still need to have a bit of tension.

00:00:51.980 --> 00:00:54.030
What exactly is Saki-chan doing there?

00:00:57.230 --> 00:00:59.630
You gotta have power to 
sing and dance too, right?

00:00:59.630 --> 00:01:01.790
And we're trying to take over 
the whole damn country.

00:01:02.130 --> 00:01:04.540
You really think exercising is 
gonna matter for zombies...?

00:01:04.770 --> 00:01:05.900
Of course it does!

00:01:05.900 --> 00:01:08.080
Think about how good Saganship worked.

00:01:08.080 --> 00:01:10.000
A little bit of work and 
I'm gonna be ripped.

00:01:13.020 --> 00:01:14.110
Down I go...

00:01:14.580 --> 00:01:15.340
Come on!

00:01:16.180 --> 00:01:17.220
And again!

00:01:16.770 --> 00:01:20.800
Saki-san has a real talent 
for pulling people along.

00:01:17.220 --> 00:01:18.420
That's the way!

00:01:18.420 --> 00:01:19.650
Oof...

00:01:19.650 --> 00:01:20.410
Again!

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:23.560
Something about her passion is infectious.

00:01:29.010 --> 00:01:31.350
Even if we have nothing else, 
we still have the future.

00:01:31.350 --> 00:01:34.200
A lowest point? Starting over from zero? 
That's just part of the saga.

00:01:34.520 --> 00:01:36.940
Even if we burn out in the process, 
we'll make it come true!

00:01:36.940 --> 00:01:39.240
This is where our revenge begins!

00:01:39.370 --> 00:01:44.370
<b>{title}Zombie Land Saga 
Revenge</b>

00:01:44.540 --> 00:01:49.670
<b>The SAGA of an Almost-Broken Radio</b>

00:02:57.720 --> 00:02:59.540
Good morning. There's been an incident.

00:03:01.530 --> 00:03:04.140
As all of Japan celebrates 
the start of the Reiwa era,

00:03:04.140 --> 00:03:09.840
a tiny portion of Saga is celebrating 
news of the return of Franchouchou.

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:10.460
Let's get some comments.

00:03:10.630 --> 00:03:13.950
Miss Four, do you have any thoughts 
to share about getting back to work?

00:03:14.770 --> 00:03:19.240
I-I think it'll be important to make 
up for the month we took off...

00:03:20.320 --> 00:03:24.060
Miss Three, what kind of activities are you 
considering to make up for the lost time?

00:03:26.670 --> 00:03:30.940
We'll still need to do our usual jobs, 
but also try new ones, right?

00:03:33.160 --> 00:03:35.740
Miss One, what would be an 
example of these new jobs?

00:03:36.630 --> 00:03:38.390
I-I dunno!

00:03:38.390 --> 00:03:39.780
Maybe acting?

00:03:47.020 --> 00:03:48.080
Or going on...

00:03:48.080 --> 00:03:49.530
Going on stage and doing comedy skits?

00:03:49.530 --> 00:03:51.700
The answer is going on TV!

00:03:52.450 --> 00:03:56.640
Right now, you need to play up 
your return to a wide audience

00:03:56.640 --> 00:03:59.250
and do it with as big an impact as possible!

00:03:59.250 --> 00:04:02.250
Bottom line is, nothing is gonna 
compare to TV for that kinda thing!

00:04:02.250 --> 00:04:04.020
You knucklehead zombie!

00:04:08.670 --> 00:04:12.130
Give it a rest! This whole damn 
mess is is your fault, anyway!

00:04:12.520 --> 00:04:15.480
That was a violation of zombie conduct 
standards, I'll have you know...

00:04:15.480 --> 00:04:17.990
Don't you have something 
you need to explain to us?

00:04:17.990 --> 00:04:21.100
Oh, this is so terrifying! 
It's zombie harassment!

00:04:21.100 --> 00:04:22.380
I'll sue!

00:04:22.380 --> 00:04:23.580
It's an abuse of zombie power dynamics!

00:04:23.580 --> 00:04:25.610
So, if you want to avoid civil court,

00:04:25.610 --> 00:04:29.000
you'd better pull off this big job that the 
great Kotaro Tatsumi landed for you all!

00:04:28.990 --> 00:04:30.950
<b>"TV Reporters"</b>

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:30.480
Ta-da!

00:04:32.300 --> 00:04:37.320
You're all going to be doing a segment on 
the tourism hotspot, Yutoku Inari Shrine!

00:04:37.630 --> 00:04:39.730
We all get to be on TV?

00:04:39.730 --> 00:04:42.340
Your Pappy might even get to see you.

00:04:42.520 --> 00:04:45.080
And this isn't just any segment...

00:04:45.930 --> 00:04:48.400
There's going to be an additional guest.

00:04:48.720 --> 00:04:51.630
<i>The</i> White Ryu is going to be there, too!

00:04:52.880 --> 00:04:54.360
White... who?

00:04:55.070 --> 00:04:56.580
White Ryu!

00:04:56.440 --> 00:04:57.770
<b>White Ryu</b>

00:04:57.770 --> 00:04:59.540
In addition to his music career,

00:04:59.540 --> 00:05:02.250
he was also the host of a late-night 
radio program that started in 1992,

00:05:02.250 --> 00:05:06.610
<i>So Saga Can Be Saga</i>, which was 
popular all over the country.

00:05:06.610 --> 00:05:09.900
He's a Saga-bred legendary rock star!

00:05:09.900 --> 00:05:14.000
The answers you're looking for 
can all be found in Saga!

00:05:15.070 --> 00:05:16.870
You're talking about <i>the</i> Ryu-san!

00:05:17.080 --> 00:05:20.270
Indeed. It's been thirty years 
since he made his debut,

00:05:20.270 --> 00:05:23.880
but he continues to broadcast his 
message to the youth from Saga!

00:05:25.520 --> 00:05:26.980
He's so damn awesome!

00:05:26.980 --> 00:05:30.100
I didn't know we had a 
celebrity like that in Saga.

00:05:30.100 --> 00:05:31.520
You wanna die?

00:05:32.730 --> 00:05:34.210
Listen up, people!

00:05:34.210 --> 00:05:39.230
Get out there, show people you're back,
 and schmooze with a real Saga legend!

00:05:39.500 --> 00:05:41.190
When?! When's this happening?!

00:05:42.650 --> 00:05:44.900
Right now!

00:05:49.110 --> 00:05:52.090
If you take a stroll through
the shopping district,

00:05:52.090 --> 00:05:54.200
you'll get a nice view of the shrine.

00:05:54.520 --> 00:05:58.290
We'll have some nice cue cards for you, 
so we're counting on you for a nice job.

00:05:58.610 --> 00:06:00.810
I-It's a pleasure to work with you!

00:06:17.010 --> 00:06:19.320
Huh... He looks different...

00:06:31.620 --> 00:06:32.860
Sorry about the holdup.

00:06:33.420 --> 00:06:36.780
The wind blowing down from 
Kyogatake gave me pause.

00:06:37.970 --> 00:06:39.800
It's really him! No doubt about it!

00:06:41.190 --> 00:06:42.450
Lame.

00:06:42.750 --> 00:06:44.250
<b>Do a nice job</b>

00:06:44.420 --> 00:06:46.300
H-Hello, everyone!

00:06:46.300 --> 00:06:49.870
This is Franchouchou,
 and we're back on the scene again.

00:06:49.870 --> 00:06:54.400
Today, we're here at Yutoku
 Inari Shrine with White Ryu-san!

00:06:54.400 --> 00:06:58.310
Um, do you visit places like this often?

00:06:58.580 --> 00:07:01.290
If you're asking me, the answer's yes.

00:07:01.880 --> 00:07:06.550
But if you're asking the winds 
of Saga... the answer's yes.

00:07:06.550 --> 00:07:07.280
Yes!

00:07:08.720 --> 00:07:10.420
Sakura, cue card!

00:07:10.990 --> 00:07:12.490
<b>Do a nice segue into going around</b>

00:07:12.620 --> 00:07:15.940
R-Right! Um... nice how?

00:07:15.080 --> 00:07:16.700
<b>Wooden Swords</b>

00:07:20.160 --> 00:07:23.170
This shopping district prides itself 
on its one-of-a-kind merchandise.

00:07:23.480 --> 00:07:26.290
Every unique shop has 
its own signature items!

00:07:26.290 --> 00:07:28.470
Wow! Let's check it out!

00:07:32.840 --> 00:07:34.350
<b>Stars of the Ariake Sea 
Mudskippers</b>

00:07:35.100 --> 00:07:37.550
Whatcha looking at, Ryu-san?

00:07:37.840 --> 00:07:38.750
Check it.

00:07:38.750 --> 00:07:41.780
These mudskippers are trapped in 
the society called an aquarium.

00:07:42.220 --> 00:07:45.190
They're just like you gals, struggling 
with the rage of being contained.

00:07:46.660 --> 00:07:48.910
For real! That's just like us!

00:07:49.330 --> 00:07:51.920
I wanna give these little 
fellas a path to freedom.

00:07:52.320 --> 00:07:53.110
How much?

00:07:53.350 --> 00:07:55.050
Those are actually my pets.

00:07:55.050 --> 00:07:58.360
You're gonna have to settle for the chopstick
rest version. They're 500 yen a piece.

00:08:03.790 --> 00:08:06.250
Freedom!

00:08:06.690 --> 00:08:09.160
You think this is nice enough?

00:08:09.160 --> 00:08:12.120
I figure they seem to be having 
a good time. It should work.

00:08:12.810 --> 00:08:14.970
That's a really colorful shrine!

00:08:14.970 --> 00:08:17.090
It's so cute, like a toy!

00:08:17.090 --> 00:08:20.480
Cuts a different figure than the 
Kurou Inari we had in Yoshiwara.

00:08:21.180 --> 00:08:22.690
<b>Have a nice chat about the marriage god</b>

00:08:23.040 --> 00:08:25.340
Um, say, Number Four?

00:08:25.340 --> 00:08:26.310
What is it?

00:08:26.310 --> 00:08:29.770
That's supposed to be a shrine for the god of marriage! Let's check it out!

00:08:29.770 --> 00:08:32.580
M-Marri—?! No, thank you!

00:08:33.030 --> 00:08:34.280
<b>Take a nice visit to the main shrine</b>

00:08:37.790 --> 00:08:40.880
You think zombie prayers count?

00:08:40.880 --> 00:08:42.940
I'm sure the gods are
 surprised we're even here.

00:08:44.250 --> 00:08:47.210
<b>Time for a nice wrap-up</b>

00:08:47.420 --> 00:08:49.850
And so, we're just about out of time.

00:08:49.850 --> 00:08:50.450
Hold it.

00:08:51.730 --> 00:08:55.690
It's true that the light shines 
on this part of Yutoku Inari,

00:08:56.680 --> 00:08:59.240
but if you let that light dazzle you,

00:08:59.240 --> 00:09:03.380
you'll never reach the destination that awaits 
those who struggle through the darkness...

00:09:05.230 --> 00:09:06.270
What do you mean?!

00:09:06.850 --> 00:09:11.280
These days, the glitz and bustle of the 
big city can cover up the truth...

00:09:12.230 --> 00:09:16.170
If you're willing to crawl to get to 
that truth, I'll show you the way.

00:09:18.320 --> 00:09:21.740
<b>Elevator   

00:09:18.320 --> 00:09:21.740
<b>Inner Temple</b>

00:09:20.410 --> 00:09:21.730
To the inner temple!

00:09:22.270 --> 00:09:23.860
The inner... temple!

00:09:24.080 --> 00:09:27.380
Uh, Ryu-san, I figure the inner temple 
is gonna make for a rougher shoot...

00:09:27.380 --> 00:09:28.120
You gotta let us go!

00:09:29.870 --> 00:09:32.160
We're free now!

00:09:33.490 --> 00:09:34.670
I figured...

00:09:39.090 --> 00:09:41.040
This is a real climb!

00:09:41.300 --> 00:09:43.900
I can only imagine how hard 
it'd be if we were alive.

00:09:44.340 --> 00:09:46.360
Just you wait, inner temple!

00:09:55.040 --> 00:09:57.550
Holy crap!

00:09:57.550 --> 00:09:59.600
You can see all the way to the Ariake Sea!

00:10:01.910 --> 00:10:04.200
Ryu-san?! You okay?!

00:10:09.830 --> 00:10:15.100
Grasping hold of something real... 
is never easy...

00:10:15.820 --> 00:10:20.100
Ryu-san!

00:10:21.500 --> 00:10:23.220
I figure that's perfect!

00:10:23.220 --> 00:10:24.530
Looks nice!

00:10:25.280 --> 00:10:29.520
The Franchouchou girls are doing a 
decent job keeping up with Ryu-san.

00:10:29.520 --> 00:10:33.550
I seriously have no idea what that 
guy's saying, even if I pay attention.

00:10:34.030 --> 00:10:36.370
Saki-chan, you can't get mad!

00:10:37.400 --> 00:10:38.610
Damn it!

00:10:41.520 --> 00:10:44.630
Ryu-san's words are like fists fulla soul!

00:10:44.630 --> 00:10:47.420
You don't use your ears! You gotta 
feel what he says in here!

00:10:50.320 --> 00:10:51.200
I gotta go!

00:10:51.200 --> 00:10:51.870
Saki-chan?!

00:10:53.010 --> 00:10:53.850
'Scuse me!

00:10:55.330 --> 00:10:59.090
Um... getting to meet you today was...

00:10:59.400 --> 00:11:01.610
I mean, you rock, Ryu-san!

00:11:01.610 --> 00:11:03.170
Thank you so much.

00:11:04.860 --> 00:11:07.140
I think we had a good wind blowing today.

00:11:07.990 --> 00:11:12.180
I haven't caught your show in a while, 
but I'm gonna listen again soon!

00:11:12.790 --> 00:11:14.360
It'll be waiting for you.

00:11:14.640 --> 00:11:15.930
Thanks!

00:11:17.570 --> 00:11:20.640
Not that I'm gonna be there
 much longer myself.

00:11:22.250 --> 00:11:24.380
Things change with time, y'know?

00:11:24.380 --> 00:11:26.430
H-Hang on a sec!

00:11:26.740 --> 00:11:28.350
That show, it's...

00:11:29.550 --> 00:11:34.310
Don't sweat it. The answers you're
looking for can still be found in Saga!

00:11:41.050 --> 00:11:46.060
<b>Zombie Land Saga Revenge</b>

00:11:46.060 --> 00:11:51.060
<b>Zombie Land Saga Revenge</b>

00:11:46.060 --> 00:11:51.060
<b>Got it~!!</b>

00:11:53.430 --> 00:11:56.470
Saki-chan's been like that 
ever since we got back...

00:11:56.830 --> 00:11:59.460
You think she liked that old guy?

00:11:59.900 --> 00:12:01.410
Th-That's...

00:12:01.410 --> 00:12:02.520
You mean romantically?

00:12:02.520 --> 00:12:03.290
Romance...

00:12:03.290 --> 00:12:05.670
It's not that weird, is it?

00:12:05.670 --> 00:12:08.670
The heart's the same, 
whether you're human or zombie.

00:12:08.890 --> 00:12:12.570
Being zombies is one thing, but we're idols!

00:12:12.570 --> 00:12:15.430
Idols aren't allowed to like someone?

00:12:16.050 --> 00:12:17.490
We're not, right?!

00:12:17.830 --> 00:12:21.790
I think it'd be fine, as long 
as it helps you shine brighter.

00:12:21.790 --> 00:12:23.150
You do?!

00:12:23.730 --> 00:12:25.920
It's hard to refute out of hand.

00:12:25.920 --> 00:12:26.970
It is?!

00:12:27.190 --> 00:12:30.720
I mean, actually getting into a 
relationship would be different...

00:12:30.980 --> 00:12:35.860
But even in your day, idols would 
get together in secret, Junko.

00:12:36.150 --> 00:12:37.870
Is that true?!

00:12:37.870 --> 00:12:39.700
Did you have a crush on somebody, Ai-chan?!

00:12:40.050 --> 00:12:42.000
Of course not!

00:12:42.000 --> 00:12:44.580
I love all of humanity,

00:12:44.580 --> 00:12:47.190
because they all love me!

00:12:47.400 --> 00:12:50.290
Make sure to include me in that number.

00:12:50.650 --> 00:12:53.530
Let's just give Saki some space for now.

00:12:57.200 --> 00:13:01.010
<i>This one's from "Saga P.D.'s Dirty Harry."</i>

00:13:01.310 --> 00:13:04.480
<i>You again, pal? "Good evening, Ryu-san."</i>

00:13:04.730 --> 00:13:10.560
<i>"Lately there's a lady working at my 
usual bar who talks all old-timey..."</i>

00:13:10.560 --> 00:13:14.760
"And from the looks she gives, 
 I think she's into me."

00:13:15.720 --> 00:13:16.560
You're all mixed up!

00:13:16.880 --> 00:13:21.330
<i>Time for a song! This one's White 
Ryu's "Do You Hate Windy Days"?</i>

00:13:21.330 --> 00:13:22.520
Saki-chan.

00:13:23.370 --> 00:13:25.440
Sorry for worrying you guys.

00:13:27.790 --> 00:13:31.140
I learned about Ryu-san when 
I was in middle school...

00:13:32.360 --> 00:13:37.070
Back then... I thought the whole 
damn world was against me.

00:13:37.860 --> 00:13:39.780
The teachers, the other students...

00:13:39.780 --> 00:13:42.740
Whenever I wouldn't take their 
crap, they tried to get rid of me.

00:13:44.760 --> 00:13:49.750
So I fought with everything I had, like it 
was the only way to prove I was out there...

00:13:51.600 --> 00:13:53.210
And that was when it happened.

00:14:02.570 --> 00:14:05.950
<i>No matter who you are, it's rough 
not knowing where you belong.</i>

00:14:07.490 --> 00:14:10.900
<i>But it's times like that you gotta 
keep your eyes, and your ears, open.</i>

00:14:11.310 --> 00:14:15.070
<i>You're gonna find somebody who 
feels the same way you do.</i>

00:14:15.530 --> 00:14:20.080
<i>Even now, me talking with you like 
this means you're not alone.</i>

00:14:20.800 --> 00:14:23.470
<i>Over time, you might forget all about me.</i>

00:14:23.850 --> 00:14:28.310
<i>But running into you like this, 
and getting to know you?</i>

00:14:28.310 --> 00:14:29.550
<i>That's something I'll never forget.</i>

00:14:30.010 --> 00:14:35.760
<i>And, if you ever feel nervous or alone, 
this'll be a place you can come back to.</i>

00:14:36.770 --> 00:14:38.410
That's mine...

00:14:50.780 --> 00:14:54.330
<i>You're gonna find somebody who 
feels the same way you do.</i>

00:14:56.540 --> 00:14:59.360
That's how I found Reiko.

00:14:59.580 --> 00:15:04.090
And now I'm a zombie,
 running with you and the others.

00:15:05.000 --> 00:15:08.180
If it wasn't for Ryu-san, who the 
hell knows what would've happened...

00:15:10.020 --> 00:15:13.180
Nah. No, I just can't accept this!

00:15:28.200 --> 00:15:30.400
Whoa, whoa, whoa, whoa!

00:15:33.080 --> 00:15:36.110
Hey, get back here! No riding double!

00:15:55.290 --> 00:15:57.890
Next up, we've got a request for an encore.

00:15:57.890 --> 00:16:01.200
White Ryu with "Do You Hate Windy Days?"

00:16:03.960 --> 00:16:05.370
'Scuse us!

00:16:12.220 --> 00:16:15.830
Two little kittens... 
but they don't look lost.

00:16:16.430 --> 00:16:19.980
Did you hear that Franchouchou was back?

00:16:20.760 --> 00:16:23.650
Yeah, they posted about it.

00:16:24.290 --> 00:16:25.990
That's disgusting, man...

00:16:28.400 --> 00:16:32.250
Okay. Seems like we've got 
a hot wind blowing today.

00:16:32.510 --> 00:16:34.180
Let me introduce you to our surprise guests.

00:16:34.570 --> 00:16:37.490
I'm Franchouchou's Number Two! 
Nice to be here!

00:16:37.810 --> 00:16:41.720
I'm F-Franchouchou's Number One! 
Sorry to intrude!

00:16:43.530 --> 00:16:45.100
So, what's up?

00:16:45.390 --> 00:16:48.150
I can't let this show end!

00:16:48.480 --> 00:16:51.840
There's plenty of folks in Saga who 
don't know what to do with themselves.

00:16:51.840 --> 00:16:54.320
Hell, Saga itself doesn't know what to do!

00:16:54.320 --> 00:16:56.480
If you quit the radio, Ryu-san...

00:16:56.480 --> 00:17:00.190
What's gonna happen to them... 
to Saga's smoldering heart?

00:17:01.060 --> 00:17:05.370
The only reason I'm an idol now 
is because I had this show!

00:17:05.790 --> 00:17:09.110
<i>There are people like me out there in Saga...</i>

00:17:09.110 --> 00:17:11.830
<i>Nah! All over Japan! There're tons of us!</i>

00:17:12.090 --> 00:17:15.460
So, I'm begging you! 
You gotta keep the show going!

00:17:15.680 --> 00:17:18.390
You need to be here for people to turn to!

00:17:18.690 --> 00:17:22.920
That's the thing. They need 
a place to turn to, not me.

00:17:24.230 --> 00:17:26.300
I wasn't just gonna split.

00:17:26.720 --> 00:17:30.140
I wanted to leave this place to someone with 
the passion in their soul to manage it...

00:17:31.210 --> 00:17:34.270
Hell, look at how droopy 
this thing's gotten.

00:17:34.530 --> 00:17:35.990
Yeah, but who—

00:17:36.410 --> 00:17:39.440
The answer is always in Saga!

00:17:41.910 --> 00:17:43.990
You gals are taking over this radio show.

00:17:47.820 --> 00:17:49.670
H-Hang on a sec...

00:17:49.670 --> 00:17:51.420
You're here right now in front of me.

00:17:51.780 --> 00:17:53.460
What more reason do I need?

00:17:54.110 --> 00:17:55.330
Ryu-san...

00:17:55.330 --> 00:17:58.460
You've got the kinda spark 
that lights a fire in folks.

00:17:59.100 --> 00:18:00.520
It's not just about Franchouchou.

00:18:01.000 --> 00:18:03.120
You're gonna be a leader to all of Saga!

00:18:06.960 --> 00:18:09.410
The leader of Franchouchou, Number Two!

00:18:09.410 --> 00:18:13.030
I'm going to be following in Ryu-san's 
footsteps, taking over this radio show!

00:18:15.820 --> 00:18:18.730
They sure seem to be settling this 
without asking anybody else...

00:18:18.730 --> 00:18:22.290
Don't blink. You'll miss seeing Saga history!

00:18:24.760 --> 00:18:27.380
Saga's in your hands now.

00:18:29.690 --> 00:18:31.950
Hey... What are you gonna do now?

00:18:33.350 --> 00:18:37.350
The wind from Kyogatake is pushing me on.

00:18:37.910 --> 00:18:39.730
It wants me to tell the 
whole world about Saga.

00:18:45.680 --> 00:18:49.400
Ryu-san... I... I love you!

00:18:52.380 --> 00:18:53.550
Don't be dumb.

00:18:54.100 --> 00:18:57.220
I'm not the one who needs 
that passion now.

00:18:58.190 --> 00:19:03.330
It's everyone who doesn't know what to do...
 No, it's Saga itself that needs you.

00:19:04.780 --> 00:19:05.710
Right.

00:19:08.500 --> 00:19:13.170
Look me up when you're a bit older 
and have grown into fine women.

00:19:30.480 --> 00:19:32.390
He was really cool, huh?

00:19:33.680 --> 00:19:38.020
I bet Reiko probably met a guy like him...

00:19:38.460 --> 00:19:40.690
He said we'd see him again, huh?

00:19:41.680 --> 00:19:44.040
When I'm a bit older, huh...

00:19:44.380 --> 00:19:45.630
Saki-chan?

00:19:46.460 --> 00:19:48.030
Except, no matter how long passes,

00:19:48.030 --> 00:19:51.450
I'm never gonna grow up... 
into a fine woman, huh?

00:19:51.810 --> 00:19:53.660
Since we're zombies!

00:19:56.780 --> 00:19:58.490
Huh? What the...?

00:20:02.680 --> 00:20:04.030
Saki-chan!

00:20:04.030 --> 00:20:06.920
Oh, what do I do, what do I do?!

00:20:10.280 --> 00:20:12.170
I don't get it, man...

00:20:37.430 --> 00:20:40.210
Come on, what're you crying for?

00:20:40.550 --> 00:20:44.040
Because... you were...!

00:20:44.510 --> 00:20:48.170
Sorry, sorry. Quit crying! Okay?

00:20:52.270 --> 00:20:54.730
You're drying up! This is seriously bad!

00:20:54.730 --> 00:20:55.970
Aw, crap, this is really bad!

00:20:56.430 --> 00:20:59.000
Come on, Sakura, you're gonna be a mummy!

00:21:01.550 --> 00:21:04.160
We heard the show! It's up to you now!

00:21:04.160 --> 00:21:06.200
We're rooting for you gals!

00:21:06.480 --> 00:21:11.330
As leader of Franchouchou, 
I've been up here letting my soul burn.

00:21:11.570 --> 00:21:14.570
From now on, so that I can lead all of Saga,

00:21:14.570 --> 00:21:17.340
my soul's gonna be blazing brighter 
than ever when I'm on stage!

00:21:17.750 --> 00:21:20.360
If I do that, no matter where they are,

00:21:20.360 --> 00:21:22.420
anyone who's lost is gonna be 
able to see my soul burning!

00:21:22.920 --> 00:21:26.680
Just like Lake Imari's breakwater 
lighthouse, over in Uranosaki!

00:21:27.220 --> 00:21:31.010
So, here we go! "Do You Hate Windy Days?"

00:21:35.970 --> 00:21:37.890
<i>I wanna see you all get fired up!</i>

00:21:37.890 --> 00:21:38.940
<i>Let's go!</i>

00:21:38.940 --> 00:21:40.820
<i>Come on and make some noise!</i>

00:21:40.820 --> 00:21:41.520
<i>Let's go!</i>

00:21:41.520 --> 00:21:43.910
<i>The whole world was your enemy</i>

00:21:43.910 --> 00:21:46.570
<i>And it had you spitting mad</i>

00:21:46.930 --> 00:21:49.980
<i>But the nights were still sweet, 
and you had the feeling</i>

00:21:49.980 --> 00:21:52.790
<i>That something wild was about to happen</i>

00:21:53.010 --> 00:21:58.420
<i>You're a lot like me, and we 
headed to the drive-in together</i>

00:21:58.420 --> 00:22:01.830
<i>And for some reason even the 
light shining in the sky</i>

00:22:01.830 --> 00:22:04.700
<i>Pissed you off enough to 
have you staring it down</i>

00:22:04.700 --> 00:22:08.750
<i>Ah, but you know,
 someday you're gonna understand</i>

00:22:10.730 --> 00:22:14.640
<i>Ah, but I know, 
someday you'll be different</i>

00:22:16.130 --> 00:22:19.150
<i>One day you'll be the kinda person who</i>

00:22:19.150 --> 00:22:22.870
<i>Can love who they used to be!</i>

00:22:23.350 --> 00:22:29.020
<i>Do you hate windy days?!</i>

00:22:29.200 --> 00:22:34.710
<i>We've got way more than this,
 don't you even joke!</i>

00:22:35.360 --> 00:22:41.620
<i>The same way that love can just be love</i>

00:22:41.620 --> 00:22:47.180
<i>You just need to be you!</i>

00:22:46.110 --> 00:22:52.180
And so, it's time to wrap up <i>So Saga 
Can Be Saga</i>, featuring Franchouchou.

00:22:50.250 --> 00:22:56.490
<i>You just need to be you!</i>

00:22:52.780 --> 00:22:57.140
If you ever feel worried or alone, 
make your way on back here.

00:22:57.140 --> 00:23:02.150
We're always gonna be on the airwaves 
for you, so don't sweat it!

00:23:02.700 --> 00:23:04.890
Keep those eyes and ears open!

00:23:05.280 --> 00:23:08.930
Take your soul in your fist, and raise it up!

00:23:12.490 --> 00:23:17.630
And don't forget: the answers you're 
looking for can always be found in Saga.

00:23:25.000 --> 00:23:25.800
<b>Next Episode Preview</b>

00:23:25.790 --> 00:23:26.570
Saki here!

00:23:26.770 --> 00:23:29.300
I'm gonna carry Saga's burning soul forward!

00:23:29.620 --> 00:23:31.270
We're gonna go for a real impact this time!

00:23:31.270 --> 00:23:34.110
Next time on <i>Zombie Land 
Saga Revenge</i> Episode 3:

00:23:34.100 --> 00:23:40.010
<b>Episode 3: The Acoustic SAGA of Love and Youth</b>

00:23:34.110 --> 00:23:36.430
"The Acoustic SAGA of Love and Youth."

00:23:36.430 --> 00:23:37.840
Check it out!
